WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.800
Start with the merchant task and the information the app needs.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:11.700
The description becomes a reviewed native app definition.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:17.800
Arrange graphical components and select their properties.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.700
The visual designer and coding agents share one versioned definition.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:29.800
Open the app assistant beside the current work.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:35.700
Use Veyndo AI, Codex or Claude Code, then review the proposed change.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:41.800
Declare the settings a merchant fills after installing the app.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:47.700
Credentials remain server side and do not become browser or agent data.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:53.800
The installed app contains a saved consultation request.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:59.700
Its product relationship, private upload and reviewed status stay connected.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:05.800
An upgrade is checked against existing app records and active consumers.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:11.700
An incompatible package is refused before replacing the installed version.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:17.700
Explore the current product and try the connected workflows.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.700
Read the handbook, open a private workspace, and review your changes.
